Description: Make mouse_warping output follow the focus across outputs, like i3
 Regolith runs both sessions with mouse_warping output. In sway the
 pointer was warped from inside the focus code on any focus change that
 left the focus on another output than the pointer, so it behaved unlike
 i3 both ways. A window opening or closing on the focused output pulled
 the pointer over from the other output, and a command that moved the
 focus away and back still warped it. Moving the focused window onto the
 other output (move left/right, or a fullscreen request naming that
 output) left the pointer behind, and focus arriving at a floating window
 that sticks out past the edge of the layout did not move it at all.
 .
 The focused output of every seat is now recorded when the outermost
 command list starts. Once it has finished, the pointer of each seat
 whose focused output changed is moved to the middle of the focused
 window or workspace, kept on that output, unless it is already there.
 Window activation and fullscreen requests from clients are handled the
 same way. While a launcher or another layer surface has the keyboard,
 the window that gets it back counts as focused. mouse_warping container
 and none are unchanged.
